Hack Braille 3.003
==================

Hack 3.003 (https://github.com/source-foundry/Hack, release v3.003,
Hack-v3.003-ttf.zip) with the Braille Patterns block U+2800..U+28FF added,
which Hack lacks and many TUIs use for graphs and spinners.  Built for the
xterm package, which compiles these fonts in and uses "Hack Braille" as its
default face.

The braille glyphs are drawn by mkhackbraille.py: 8 square dots on a 2x4
grid spanning the character cell, the geometry of the Nerd Fonts patcher's
"rectangle" braille.  No glyphs are taken from other fonts.  The fonts are
renamed to "Hack Braille" (PostScript "HackBraille-*"), as the Bitstream
Vera license requires of modified fonts.  Everything else is unchanged.

License: as Hack, see LICENSE.md (MIT for the Hack project's work, Bitstream
Vera License for the Bitstream Vera Sans Mono glyphs).  mkhackbraille.py
itself is under the MIT License (see its header).

Rebuild (needs python3 with fontTools):

    for s in Regular Bold Italic BoldItalic; do
        python3 mkhackbraille.py Hack-$s.ttf HackBraille-$s.ttf
    done

